# Settings for workstation/agent-brief. Copy to ~/.config/ziggurat/config.env
# (or point ZIGGURAT_CONFIG at it). Keep the real file private.
# The console has its own settings: see console/README.md.

# Where the console keeps pulled data, one subfolder per project
# (the same folder as FLEET_DATA in the console's compose env).
FLEET_DATA=$HOME/ziggurat-data/fleet

# Optional: where the console keeps pulled transcripts, one subfolder per
# project (<folder>/<project>/projects/...). Gives the brief the lead's own
# final report; without it the brief works from the ledger's short summary.
#TRANSCRIPTS_DATA=$HOME/ziggurat-data/transcripts

# Optional: wait this long after a cycle ends (the gate judges its work), and
# skip cycles that ended longer ago than this.
#BRIEF_SETTLE_MIN=20
#BRIEF_BACKFILL_HOURS=48

# Optional: a Python that has `edge-tts` installed, for the spoken brief.
#SPEAK_PYTHON=$HOME/ziggurat-data/venv/bin/python
# Optional: voice for the spoken brief.
#FLEET_TTS_VOICE=en-US-AndrewNeural

# Optional: push each brief's headline.
#NTFY_URL=https://ntfy.sh/<long-random-topic>
